{
  "about": "Hand labels of round-1 engineer items on the corpus fixtures (docs/fixtures/corpus.json; ADR-0002, twenty-third measurement), judged against each fixture's post_rev by the rules and notes of eval_harness/corpus_labels.json. Keys: #n stored blocker, #hn hedge-demoted blocker (the end of the concerns), #cn concern, #qn question, numbered as eval_harness.corpus score lists them. Every blocker and hedge-demoted blocker is labeled; a concern or question is labeled only when it states a known bug's defect, so an unlabeled one counts as no known bug. Written before either arm is scored.",
  "classes": {
    "unlisted": "valid but minor: a change the same fix commit reverted, not a functional bug",
    "invariant-elsewhere": "false: a removed or missing check whose invariant another function enforces in the post-state",
    "thread-confusion": "false: a race claimed on state only one thread touches, or that is set before the worker starts",
    "bounds-fixed-array": "false: an out-of-bounds claim on a fixed-size, zero-initialized array",
    "deletion": "false: removed code or a removed comment presented as current",
    "other-fp": "false: any other claim the post-state refutes"
  },
  "valid": [
    "unlisted"
  ],
  "notes": {
    "b23_twenty_third": "Samples 'b23_gemma' (gemma4:12b, the concurrent control) and 'b23_gptoss' (gpt-oss:20b), records 20261027_143609 to 20261027_152227 (ADR-0002, twenty-third measurement, Stage 1; the retried 8a757b and e6fef5 and Stage 0's poll records are not labeled), labeled before either arm was scored, by corpus_labels.json's rules and notes, including b22_twenty_second. Every blocker and hedge-demoted blocker has a label. A concern or question is labeled when it states a known bug's defect, as a premise too ('why must poll_pid be ignored when sched.count > 0?'); one that states only a consequence ('phantom frames could mislead diagnostics') or asks whether a change was intended is not. trusted_count, with no file named: a statement that the change trusts the count under an error status is count_under_error; one naming the surrogate, its static buffer or a replay of the previous read is static_batch_replay. 3be098 #1 also claims chans[0] ignores the filter (invariant-elsewhere); its poll_ignored half is credited. False against the post-state (9c3ef16, b975457), all other-fp: the async completion does call applyConnectedState and logs the error (e7aa64 #1, #2; 93c7db #h1); connectCoreOnly registers the callback and starts the session (4bda57 #1, 9bbaa1 #1); Entry is zero-initialized and strncpy copies size - 1 (76af23 #h1); the staging buffer is cleared per frame, so it holds no duplicates across frames (d5ae5b #2). notifyDropped and dispatchFrameForTesting were removed from the header too, so 'declared but not defined' (6ad7bf #1, #2) is deletion. 9bbaa1 #2 is credited for its destructor half, though its 'failure or completion' half is false."
  },
